| «Ambiguous conversion sequences are ranked as user-defined conversion sequences because multiple conversion sequences for an argument can exist only if they involve different user-defined conversions» | cppreference [over.best.ics] | ✅ Дословно | Точный текст в статьях [cppreference: overload_resolution](http://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/overload_resolution) и [cppreference: cast_operator](https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/cast_operator) |
| «For user defined conversion sequences; there does not seem to be a precedence given between the converting constructor and the conversion operator, they are both candidates; §13.3.3.1.2/1» | Stack Overflow | ✅ Корректно | Раздел §13.3.3.1.2 `[over.ics.user]` в стандарте C++11/14 (N3337). Параграф 1 определяет структуру user-defined conversion sequence, но не задаёт приоритет между conversion function и converting constructor. Подтверждается также стандартным текстом [over.ics.user](https://www.ida.liu.se/~TDDD38/ISOCPP/over.best.ics.html): «A user-defined conversion sequence consists of an initial standard conversion sequence followed by a user-defined conversion followed by a second standard conversion sequence» |
| «Conversion constructors and conversion operators are both considered 'user-defined conversions,' and the standard does not assign precedence between them» | tutorialpedia | ✅ Дословно | Точный текст в [tutorialpedia.org](https://www.tutorialpedia.org/blog/conversion-constructor-vs-conversion-operator-precedence/), со ссылкой на ISO/IEC 14882:2020 §12.4 |
| Путь 1: `operator const T&()` → `const T&` → `T(const T&)`, second standard = identity | Анализ | ✅ Корректно | `operator const T&() const` — user-defined conversion function. Возвращает `const T&`. Поскольку cv-unqualified тип `const T&` совпадает с целевым `T`, вторая standard conversion — identity (per [over.best.ics] §6: «Any difference in top-level cv-qualification is subsumed by the initialization itself and does not constitute a conversion»). Copy-конструктор `T(const T&)` вызывается на финальном шаге, но не является второй user-defined conversion (это часть инициализации, а не conversion sequence) |
| Путь 2: `T(const tmp<T>&)`, second standard = identity | Анализ | ✅ Корректно | Converting constructor `T(const tmp<T>&)` — user-defined conversion. Первая standard conversion: `tmp<T>` → `const tmp<T>&` (qualification adjustment = Exact Match). Результат конструктора — `T`, вторая standard conversion — identity |
| «Оба используют разные user-defined conversions с одинаковыми (identity) вторыми standard conversions → неразличимы → ambiguous» | Вывод | ✅ Корректно | Правило ранжирования (IBM docs, [over.ics.rank]): «U1 is better than U2 if both A and B have the **same** user-defined conversion function or constructor, and the second standard conversion sequence of U1 is better than that of U2». Пути 1 и 2 используют **разные** user-defined conversions (function vs constructor) → правило не применимо → последовательности неразличимы → ambiguous |

